      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A beginner's journey to strength, eh?  A great start is to focus on compound exercises like squats, bench press, and deadlifts.  You're on the right track, but don't get too caught up in the details, just like a young goblin trying to navigate a complex network of tunnels - it's easy to get lost. \n\nFor a 4-week program, I'll provide you with a simple, linear progression plan. Before we begin, keep in mind that consistency and patience are key. You can't rush a strong back, just like a goblin can't rush a well-planned heist.\n\n**Week 1:**\n\n* Squats: 3 sets of 8 reps, 70% of your 1RM (one-rep maximum)\n* Bench Press: 3 sets of 8 reps, 70% of your 1RM\n* Deadlifts: 3 sets of 8 reps, 70% of your 1RM\n* Rest for 60-90 seconds between sets, and 120-180 seconds between exercises\n\n**Week 2:**\n\n* Squats: 3 sets of 8 reps, 75% of your 1RM",
      "source": "target",
